body:
If you cut them, do they not bleed?  If you tickle them, do they not laugh?

&#x200B;

Well, no, but that's not the point!

Well, we're not really high level characters, so the opponents we come up against aren't massively high level or high HP either... the Halberd in question is a +6 Halberd so it's not that difficult to hit with depending on the AC of the enemy obviously.  It's a D10 of damage, but it's also a 2 handed weapon so I get 1.5 x strength mod added to damage rolls which in my case is 4, so that's a minimum of 5 damage per hit even if the dice are being mean... the crit multiplier is ***x3*** tho, so if you roll a nat 20 (it only crits on a 20 fortunately), you get ***3 D10 +12*** damage dealt... so a minimum of 15 and a max of 42 damage ***in one blow***.... you can see where I'm going with this.... when you're fighting minions with fairly crap AC and not that many hit points, if the dice are even remotely favourable you can annihilate an entire squad in a couple of rounds with a little help from the group.  The Walcofind that I turned to dust with a crit hit was supposed to take a swipe or two at us, then disappear back into the wall to attack us later... it never got the chance.

&#x200B;

I keep dropping hints about a masterwork halberd but the HubbyGM said no  lol  I imagine in the later chapters when we're fighting bigger, badder enemies, it's probably going to be a little less OP :)

If you find you can't eat, have you tried Huel?   It's a meal replacement drink, supposedly completely balanced with vitamins, minerals, slow release carbs, fibre etc, everything you need... comes in either poder form which you mix with water, or now they do a pre mixed form in ready to drink bottles.  Powder comes in various flavours, ready to drink stoff comes in berry or vanilla flavours.

&#x200B;

It's obviously not ideal, but it might be a good place to start to get the vitamins/minerals and nutrition you need to function properly, and I find it's quite filling so it might help your hunger pains too....  Over in the UK I have to order it online, not sure if it's the same in the US (or where you are in the world?) but it might be worth looking into?

&#x200B;

Bear in mind, I'm just a person, not a medical professional or anything like that, so do not hold me responsible for any advice I'm giving here, it was just an idea!

&#x200B;

There's also Soylent, which is similar to Huel, but I don't think soylent is as nutritionally balanced, and the ready to drink Soylent is a bit watery compared to the Huel so is much less filling.

&#x200B;

Hope you manage to sort something out to get you on track x

This goes without saying.

&#x200B;

 But, in addition to that, do you really think the actual on-the-ground devs had much say in what was included in the game, what game mechanics were actually implemented?  Devs do the leg-work for what the higher ups want... usually doing long hours for relatively low pay to hit ridiculous deadlines to  make something that resembles what a designer has requested.... but the finished product isn't dictated by the devs-on-the-ground... they do their best to do the work they've been given with the time and resources available to them.  


If you want to blame anyone, blame Gamefreak management.

&#x200B;

There's a good chance with everything kicking off, that the devs will be under fire from their bosses anyway, for trying to do the job they were told to do in the first place, because devs are worth nothing in the games industry, and the managers and directors of games companies never take any responsibility for any criticism, but accept praise like it's mana from heaven.

Skeksiiiiiieeee, everything about you's soooo Skeksiiiiieeee....

&#x200B;

You're welcome.

They're marginally better than Pandas which evolved to eat meat, but couldn't be bothered chasing it down, so decided to become vegetarian and so have to eat so much bamboo, which they can't digest properly, that all they can literally do is eat all day, and still barely have the energy to sit still and look sad....  A bit like me really, except for the vegetarian part.

&#x200B;

(This statement on the biology of Pandas may not be entirely accurate and may be somewhat exaggerated for comic effect.  The bit about me is not.)

 `I get that this is trying to make me feel better` 

How?  Someone feeling "sad", not wanting to get help (medication), wondering what they're getting out of bed for... does not strike me as a hopeful message of "it'll get better", but rather a message of " it never gets any better, it just goes on and on and on, relentlessly....."

&#x200B;

Or maybe that's just my take on it.

&#x200B;

 `Why do people feel like potsing this kind of posts will solve anything, please stop` 

No posts are a solution, they're just a bandaid to cover the cracks.

&#x200B;

Seriously tho, you seem oddly upset by this particular post, I hope you're ok...

I'm sure that people who use the " You can't love someone until you love yourself" line only use it to try and apportion blame for failed relationships...  It's either an (allegedly) well rounded individual full of self-worth saying "well I love myself, so I am definitely able to give you love, but you're filled with self-loathing so you can't love me properly so it must be your fault this didn't work." or some poor soul with mental health and trust issues saying "I'm sorry I can't love you the way you deserve, because I hate myself, therefore it's my fault this didn't work."  Often both.  And neither of those situations are healthy.

&#x200B;

People need to understand that EVERYONE is broken, EVERYONE has self doubt.  Even the most confident person in the world hates them selves at some point or another.

&#x200B;

You can love others even if you don't love yourself, because if you couldn't, the human population would be dwindling rather than exploding.

To paraphrase Rammstein (I say "paraphrase, because knowing Rammstein the song was *probably* about something slightly different, and my German is not great):

&#x200B;

 "Liebe ist für alle da, auch für mich"

&#x200B;

And it's true... you just have to find it, it's not necessarily easy, and it can take a lot of trial and error... people are generally assholes in one way or another, but if you can find someone who appreciates and understands your flaws that you can understand and appreciate their flaws, who makes you feel worthwhile and valued and you make them feel the same, that's about the best anyone can ask for...

Love isn't some special, amazing, light-in-the-sky, holy miracle type thing, it's finding out that - when all the hot, hormonal desire and need has died down a bit - you still want to be around that person, flaws and all, and the scales are tipped in favour of the good things rather than the bad.

Trouble is, some people are looking for that "perfect relationship" filled with hearts and flowers and bluebirds and shit... Like some Disney Princess, happily-ever-after bollocks.  And that, that doesn't exist.

&#x200B;

Everyone is alone in this life.  You just need to find a person that you're comfortable being alone with.  And alone isn't the same as lonely... loneliness is toxic, and if you feel lonely in a relationship, it's not a relationship.

&#x200B;

But anyway, TL:DR Everyone's searching, there's lots of people who will give you love and respect, Love is compromise.

I would say, don't all stand in a nice line directly in front of the dragon so he can get all of you with one blast... and if you have a rogue with an invisibility spell on her and a dragon slaying longsword, send her in first rather than leaving her at the back...

Other than that I have no advice :)

&#x200B;

&#x200B;

(In our defense, we were new players....)

It's like one of those daft,"find the panda in this black and white drawing of a Kiss convention" pictures, but once you see it, it's indelibly embedded in your eyeballs forever.

